---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";

const title = "Destinations | Portugal Considered";
const description =
  "Explore Portugal by region, from Porto and the Douro Valley to Lisbon, Central Portugal, the Algarve, Alentejo, Madeira, and beyond.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="destinations-intro">
    <div class="destinations-intro-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Explore Portugal</p>

      <h1>Where in Portugal should you go?</h1>

      <p class="intro">
        Portugal rewards travelers who choose carefully rather than try to
        see everything. Start with the regions that fit the kind of trip you
        want to take, then decide how much time each one deserves.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="destinations-section">
    <article class="destination-feature">
      <div class="destination-image">
        <img
          src="/images/alto-douro-vineyards-river.jpg"
          alt="Terraced vineyards overlooking the Douro River in northern Portugal"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="destination-content">
        <p class="region-label">Northern Portugal</p>

        <h2>Porto &amp; the Douro Valley</h2>

        <p>
          Porto brings together historic neighborhoods, riverfront life,
          architecture, food, and wine. Travel east and the Douro Valley
          changes the pace with terraced vineyards, river journeys, villages,
          and wine country.
        </p>

        <p>
          The important decisions are not simply what to see, but how to divide
          your time between city and valley, whether the Douro should be a day
          trip or an overnight stay, and whether you need a car at all.
        </p>

        <p class="status-note">
          Our first Portugal Considered guides begin here.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="destination-feature destination-feature-reverse">
      <div class="destination-image">
        <img
          src="/images/sintra-pena-palace-travelers.jpg"
          alt="Visitors exploring Pena Palace in Sintra, Portugal"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="destination-content">
        <p class="region-label">Lisbon &amp; surrounding region</p>

        <h2>Lisbon &amp; Central Portugal</h2>

        <p>
          Lisbon can anchor an entire Portugal trip, but the choices extend
          well beyond the city. Sintra, Cascais, the Atlantic coast, and
          destinations farther into Central Portugal can all compete for
          limited vacation time.
        </p>

        <p>
          Good planning means deciding what deserves a day trip, what deserves
          an overnight stay, and when Lisbon remains the most practical base.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="destination-feature">
      <div class="destination-image">
        <img
          src="/images/algarve-praia-do-camilo.jpg"
          alt="Atlantic coastline and cliffs at Praia do Camilo in the Algarve"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="destination-content">
        <p class="region-label">More of Portugal</p>

        <h2>Beyond the Two Cities</h2>

        <p>
          Portugal does not end with Porto and Lisbon. The Algarve offers
          beaches, cliffs, towns, and Atlantic scenery. Alentejo brings a
          slower landscape of historic towns, countryside, and wine, while
          Madeira offers an entirely different island experience.
        </p>

        <p>
          As Portugal Considered grows, this is where we will help travelers
          decide which of these regions belong in their trip—and which may be
          better saved for another visit.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="planning-callout">
    <div class="planning-callout-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Start with the decision</p>

      <h2>Not sure where to begin?</h2>

      <p>
        Choosing destinations is only part of the plan. How many days you have,
        how you want to travel, and how often you are willing to change bases
        can completely change which parts of Portugal make sense.
      </p>

      <a href="/trip-planning/">Explore trip planning →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .destinations-intro {
    padding: 90px 28px 80px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .destinations-intro-inner {
    max-width: 850px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .region-label {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-green);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: clamp(44px, 6vw, 68px);
    line-height: 1.08;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .intro {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 28px auto 0;
    font-size: 20px;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .destinations-section {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 20px 28px 80px;
  }

  .destination-feature {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(0, 0.9fr);
    gap: 60px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 65px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-sand);
  }

  .destination-feature-reverse .destination-image {
    order: 2;
  }

  .destination-feature-reverse .destination-content {
    order: 1;
  }

  .destination-image img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 390px;
    display: block;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .region-label {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }

  .destination-content h2,
  .planning-callout h2 {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 44px);
    line-height: 1.12;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .destination-content p {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    font-size: 17px;
  }

  .status-note {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-green);
  }

  .planning-callout {
    padding: 75px 28px 80px;
    background: var(--color-sand);
  }

  .planning-callout-inner {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .planning-callout p {
    font-size: 18px;
  }

  .planning-callout a {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .planning-callout a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .destination-feature {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 30px;
      padding: 50px 0;
    }

    .destination-feature-reverse .destination-image,
    .destination-feature-reverse .destination-content {
      order: initial;
    }

    .destination-image img {
      height: 320px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .destinations-intro {
      padding: 65px 22px 55px;
    }

    .intro {
      font-size: 18px;
    }

    .destinations-section {
      padding: 10px 22px 55px;
    }

    .destination-feature {
      padding: 42px 0;
    }

    .destination-image img {
      height: 250px;
    }

    .destination-content p {
      font-size: 16px;
    }

    .planning-callout {
      padding: 55px 22px 60px;
    }
  }
</style>
